// Signing configuration for every target in this project.
//
// Attached to the two *project-level* build configurations rather than to each
// target's, because no target sets DEVELOPMENT_TEAM of its own. A value here is
// therefore inherited by all six, and stays inherited by a seventh that nobody
// has thought of yet — which is the failure this file is really guarding
// against, since a target added later would otherwise be signed by omission.
//
// The team identifier itself is deliberately not in this file. It is a property
// of whoever is building, not of the source, so it lives in Local.xcconfig,
// which is gitignored. Copy Local.xcconfig.example to get started.
//
// The `?` makes the include optional: with no Local.xcconfig present,
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is simply unset and the project builds exactly as it did
// before this file existed. That is what keeps ./scripts/verify-apple.sh and CI
// working on a machine that has no Apple Developer account at all.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
